    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d978">

                <pb facs="0863" n="747" xml:id="pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/218.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-15T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1912—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is impossible for the arms and ammunition committee of the American colony
                    organisation to secure sufficient arms and ammunition for their purposes. They
                    have formally requested me to ascertain from our Government whether 500 rifles,
                    with necessary ammunition, can be sold, loaned or given to the organization,
                    and, if sold, at what price. Are there not some Krag-Jorgensens out of use at
                    San Antonio? The governor of the Federal District is well disposed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
